Package: trama.github
Title: GitHub Connection for trama
Version: 0.2.2
Authors@R: person("Pedro", "Mambelli Fernandes", , "pedromambelli@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Connects trama to GitHub without git or a terminal: account
    guide, login by the OAuth device flow, reuse of existing credentials,
    token kept in the system keyring, and an internal API to create
    repositories and make atomic commits and tags through the Git data API.
    It is a trama plugin, not a block collection: it has no nodes. When
    installed, the trama editor shows a GitHub menu.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    trama (>= 0.5.21),
    gitcreds,
    httr2 (>= 1.0.0),
    jsonlite,
    keyring,
    later,
    openssl,
    shiny,
    stats,
    utils
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    webfakes,
    withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/trama/plugin: true
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
